stutils/ — same\n\nFor required_reading, I'll list the paths the stitch agent should read. If I'm not sure of exact file names within a directory, I'll list the directory.\n\nActually, the constraint says required_reading should be \"Files the agent must read before starting.\" I should be specific about files, not directories. But I don't know the exact file names in pkg/sys/ and pkg/testutils/ since I can't read the filesystem.\n\nI know from the package_contracts section that:\n- pkg/testutils has exports like DiffTest, RunDiffTests, etc.\n- pkg/sys has InstallSIGPIPEHandler, etc.\n\nBut the actual file names... from P7: \"if the primary type is DiffTest, the file is difftest.go\". So pkg/testutils/difftest.go\n\nFor pkg/sys, the primary types are FileInfo, Stat, InstallSIGPIPEHandler. The SRD is srd002-sys. What would the primary file be? The primary exported type might be FileInfo, so fileinfo.go? Or since there are multiple exports, it might be split across files. Without knowing, I'll reference the directory.\n\nActually, the stitch agent really needs the SRD file most of all — that's where the requirements live. It can learn the calling patterns from CLAUDE.md, which is already in its context. So I'll focus on listing the SRD and the key package directories.\n\nI'm settling on:\n- SRD files (mandatory)\n- cmd/ reference implementations\n- pkg/testutils/difftest.go (for test patterns)\n- pkg/sys/ (directory, since I don't know the exact file structure)\n\nFor nl R1.1-R1.4, I need the SRD and reference patterns from existing commands.\n\nFor nl R2.1-R2.4, I'll reference the nl implementation and tests from the contract task, plus the SRD.\n\nI'm also noting that the stitch agent will need to read the SRD to understand what flags nl supports when creating the contract stubs.\n\nFor design decisions, I'll include the SIGPIPE handler and differential testing approach.\n\nThe reference binary for nl is gnl following the Homebrew GNU coreutils naming convention, an